---
title: "generate_token POST /v1/integration/token (Legion Backend API)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_auth: api_key = headers["x-api-key"]
    q_auth --> q_check_key: api_key valid
    q_check_key --> q_sign_body: signature = HMAC_SHA256(secret_key, body)
    q_check_key --> q_reject: api_key invalid
    q_reject --> [*]: revert "unauthorized"
    q_sign_body --> q_send: POST /v1/integration/token with X-Signature
    q_send --> q_parse: response = server_response
    q_parse --> q_extract_jwt: response.status == 2xx
    q_parse --> q_error: response.status != 2xx
    q_extract_jwt --> q_store: jwt_token = response.body.token
    q_store --> [*]: return jwt_token
    q_error --> [*]: revert "token generation failed"

    note right of q_extract_jwt
        INV-001: JWT token is returned only after valid API key + HMAC signature verification
        INV-002: JWT token has an expiration time (no refresh mechanism documented)
        INV-003: token must be stored securely client-side
        INV-004: no token revocation endpoint documented - token valid until expiry
    end note
